# Vauxhall Astra Mk2 five-door hatchback, 1984-1991.
#
# The second Astra: the Opel Kadett E twin, launched October 1984, Car of the Year
# 1985; 4,003 mm long, 1,663 mm wide, 1,390 mm high, 2,520 mm wheelbase.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opel_Kadett#Kadett_E_(1984%E2%80%931991)
#
# Colours: Carmine Red, Astro Silver, White Gold and Helios Blue are documented
# Vauxhall colours of the period.
#
# Weight: 280 in total (blue 90, red 70, silver 65, white 55), the Astra becoming
# a top-three UK seller in this generation.
#
# Speed 160 km/h; comfort 95/473 (line). Classes 0,1.
# Dates: 1984-1991 with a road tail to about 1999.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-astra-mk2.blend. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-astra-mk2/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia
# Commons.

obj=citycar
name=VauxhallAstraMk2(HeliosBlue)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=90
intro_year=1984
intro_month=10
retire_year=1999
retire_month=6
speed=160
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=95
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=473

